    "number": 211,
    "title": "Simulate the denied clipboard in the guide browser check",
    "body": "Refs #210\n\n## Summary\n\n`docs/work-guide/work/check_guide.cjs`: the task-brief check now simulates the denied clipboard in the page, stubbing `navigator.clipboard.writeText` to reject with `NotAllowedError`, the same way the existing missing-clipboard case removes the API. The real granted-clipboard copy check is unchanged. The comment explains why the check doesn't rely on the browser's default permission.\n\n## Why\n\nMain's Work guide job failed on `a19a62e` with `AssertionError: A denied clipboard selects the prompt` (check runs 107425147844 and 107426083706). The check produced its \"denied\" case with `clearPermissions()`, expecting headless Chromium to reject `writeText`. A probe with CI's Playwright 1.63.0 (Chromium 153.0.8010.12) shows `clipboard-write` reports `granted` by default and after `clearPermissions()`. The copy succeeds with \"Copied.\", so the fallback never runs.\n\nThe guide's behavior is correct: a rejected write selects the prompt and shows the manual-copy message. Only the test's assumption was wrong. #209 (Refs #196) added the check as a guide-only change, so Depot never ran it before merge.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Base: `a19a62eb673fd17a5aecdb1db6b5575947e2feb7` (origin/main). Head: `efa4f5a35e3992144be457411c31f2e21b966810`. Merge-base: the base.\n- Diff: `git diff a19a62eb673fd17a5aecdb1db6b5575947e2feb7...efa4f5a35e3992144be457411c31f2e21b966810`. Complete changed-file list: `docs/work-guide/work/check_guide.cjs` (modified). No deletions or renames.\n- **Red:** at the base, `check_guide.cjs` with Playwright 1.63.0 failed at `check_guide.cjs:214` with the same assertion as CI.\n- **Green, locally at the head:**\n  - `build_guide.py` ran with no output drift (`git diff --exit-code -- docs/work-guide/outputs`).\n  - `test_maintenance.py` reported OK.\n  - `check_guide.cjs` exited 0 with Playwright 1.63.0 / Chromium 153.0.8010.12, and also with the older local 1.62.1 runtime.\n  - Receipt checked at 2026-09-23T23:48:22Z: `taskBriefs: passed`, HTML SHA-256 `04f2214bdf17fdbc7fbeea20cbb31569cba8814a6ab7511fa986f65c6dcab234` (850,642 bytes).\n  - Screenshots, print check, receipt and red and green logs are retained outside Git in the canonical checkout's `.local/evidence/gh-210-guide-clipboard-check/`.\n- **Green, on Depot at the head:** `depot ci run --workflow .depot/workflows/work-guide.yml --job guide` created run `k88821sn49`, Sha `efa4f5a`, trigger `api`. Every step passed: build, output-drift check, maintenance tests, system design check, the guide browser check (`taskBriefs: passed`, `errors: []`) and system-design navigation.\n- **Guide-only CI exception:** every changed path is under `docs/work-guide/`. Both Depot workflows (`ci.yml`, `work-guide.yml`) use `paths-ignore: ['docs/work-guide/**']` for `pull_request` and main `push` at this candidate, so no PR or main-push Depot runs are expected. The explicit Depot run above replaces the absent PR run for the failing job. The next non-guide merge to main runs the Work guide job, and that result closes #210 and unblocks #207.\n\n## Scope notes\n\n- Test-only change: no guide content, snapshot, generated output or UI change, and no OpenSpec change.\n- Guide UI needs no human approval under the SDLC UI approval scope, and this PR changes none.\n- Related: #196 / #209 (origin of the check) and #207 (blocked on main's Work guide result).\n\n## Reviews\n\nIndependent Standards and Specification reviews pending.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
